5. SOURCE URL AND ATTRIBUTION
================================================================

When sharing licensed materials, including
modified versions, recipients must comply with
the attribution requirements of CC BY 4.0.

These include, as applicable:

- Retaining supplied creator identification.
- Retaining designated attribution-party information.
- Retaining the applicable copyright notice.
- Providing the CC BY 4.0 license information.
- Retaining a URI or hyperlink to the licensed
  material to the extent reasonably practicable.
- Indicating modifications where applicable.
- Retaining applicable modification notices.

Attribution may be provided in a reasonable manner
appropriate to the medium, means and context.

The preferred original source reference is the
exact URL of the material actually reused.

The repository URL identifies the LOYAL OS RUNTIME
project as a whole.

The official website identifies the principal
publication domain and operating organization.

