10. ORIGINAL SOURCE PROVENANCE
================================================================

LOYAL OS maintains distinctions among:

Original Creator:
The person responsible for originating the work.

Operating Organization:
The organization associated with the publication.

Original Source:
The exact URL identifying the reused material.

Canonical Entity Identifier:
The persistent identifier used to represent an entity.

Research DOI:
The identifier assigned to an individual publication.

Publication Date:
The initial publication date of the source.

Modification Date:
The latest documented modification date.

Applicable License:
The license governing the corresponding material.

These distinctions support consistent source
identification across public research systems.

